1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,860
Across global geopolitics and maritime security, no geographical chokepoint wields as much raw

2
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:08,540
leverage as the Strait of Hormuz.

3
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:13,240
Separating the rocky shores of Iran from the Arabian Peninsula, this strategic passage

4
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:17,780
narrows to barely 21 nautical miles at its critical gateway.

5
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:23,379
Every single day, over 21 million barrels of petroleum and liquefied natural gas traverse

6
00:00:23,379 --> 00:00:29,580
these waters, accounting for more than 20 percent of total global petroleum consumption.

7
00:00:29,579 --> 00:00:34,679
Under international maritime law and the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea, transit

8
00:00:34,679 --> 00:00:40,679
passage is technically guaranteed, yet sovereign posturing and naval mine capabilities create

9
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:42,739
an enduring flashpoint.

10
00:00:42,739 --> 00:00:47,640
For the superpowers and global markets alike, any disruption in these contested waters

11
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:52,840
would immediately trigger catastrophic global energy inflation and economic paralysis.

